# Line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks files out with CRLF, which is harmless
# for source but not for files a Linux container reads verbatim. dagent/Dockerfile
# writes its entrypoint with `printf`, so a checked-out `\r` would end up inside
# the generated shell script — a `/bin/sh\r` shebang, failing at container start
# with an error that names neither git nor line endings.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*/Dockerfile    text eol=lf
